Year = {2024},
Volume = {32},
Number = {1},
Abstract = {With the increasing educational level and technology usage among the
   general public, awareness regarding investment options has increased.
   The general public can be seen actively participating in the investment
   market. With increasing number of investors and their varied interests
   and reasons for investing, it is important for organisations to
   understand the investors' perception and accordingly plan the financial
   communication strategies. Decision-making is a process that is affected
   by various factors and an understanding of how these factors affect
   investors helps an organisation to communicate effectively with the
   stakeholder. The present study is an attempt to analyse the effect of
   financial communication practices on investors' risk perception and
   decision-making.},
